#. Tag: title
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kded5</command> consolidates several small services in one process. "
"These are mostly D-Bus services provided by KDED modules, but it also "
"manages sycoca (a binary cache of servicetypes, mimetypes and services used "
"by KService) and KConfig update scripts as needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For sycoca, it monitors the directories containing .desktop files. When a "
"file is added/removed, it waits 5 seconds (in case of a series of updates), "
"and then launches <command>kbuildsycoca5</command> to update the sycoca."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For KConfig, it checks newly-installed update files, i.e. the *.upd files "
"used to update configuration files of users when the configuration file "
"formats changes, and runs the KConfig update utility to perform the updates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Those tasks are also run when <command>kded5</command> is started to ensure "
"that the user configuration is up to date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You do not normally need to run <command>kded5</command> directly; Plasma "
"desktop sessions run it automatically, and it is started on demand when an "
"application attempts to use a D-Bus interface provided by it or one of its "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "--check"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check the sycoca database, updating it if necessary, and exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kded5</command> can be configured with the <filename>kded5rc</"
"filename> ini-style configuration file. On Unix systems, this can be found "
"at <filename><varname>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME</varname>/kded5rc</filename>; if "
"<varname>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME</varname> is not set, this defaults to "
"<filename>~/.config/kded5rc</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configuration file entries are read on-demand, so changes can be made while "
"<command>kded5</command> is running. However, all the current configuration "
"options only really affect the startup behaviour of <command>kded5</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <option>[General]</option> section has the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "CheckSycoca"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether to update sycoca at startup (default: <constant>true</constant>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "CheckUpdates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether to perform outstanding KConfig updates at startup (default: "
"<constant>true</constant>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "CheckFileStamps"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether to check file timestamps when performing the initial sycoca update "
"(default: <constant>true</constant>). See the documentation for "
"<command>kbuildsycoca5</command> for more details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "DelayedCheck"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether to delay the initial sycoca update until about a minute after "
"starting (default: <constant>false</constant>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each module also has a <option>[Module-<replaceable>name</replaceable>]</"
"option> section in <filename>kded5rc</filename>, where <replaceable>name</"
"replaceable> is the name of the module's desktop file without the <filename>."
"desktop</filename> extension. This contains an <option>autoload</option> "
"option that specifies whether the module should be automatically loaded when "
"<command>kded5</command> is started (default: <constant>false</constant>). "
"Note that this setting can also be changed via <command>kded5</command>'s D-"
"Bus interface."
msgstr ""

